  "title": "CRYPTO and PROVIDE EEG Baseline Data",
  "description": "This dataset comprises resting-state EEG recordings collected from Bangladeshi children as part of the CRYPTO and PROVIDE studies. The data include baseline EEG measurements from two age cohorts: 36-month-old toddlers and 6-month-old infants, acquired during a 2-minute passive viewing task. These recordings were used to investigate associations between nutritional stunting and brain functional connectivity patterns in early childhood development.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were collected from two age groups: 36-month-old toddlers (participant ID < 2000) and 6-month-old infants (participant ID > 2000). Participants viewed screen savers for 2 minutes during passive recording. Baseline EEG measurements were acquired as part of the CRYPTO and PROVIDE studies conducted in Bangladesh.",
